  (text "eth0 stays on 192.168.1.100 and the phone hotspot must not.\nThe sensor never touches the GPIO header -- it is Ethernet\nthe whole way. TB1 inside U7 takes the VLP-16 factory cable:\n1 Gnd/Shield, 2 +12 Vdc, 3 GPS_Pulse_CNT, 4 GPS_RX_CNT,\n5 Eth TX+, 6 Eth TX-, 7 Eth RX+, 8 Eth RX-, 9 GPS return." (exclude_from_sim yes) (at 386.08 227.35 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid "9cda15f9-ec27-53a5-b2e6-fe69f30bc050"))
  (text "ACCEPTANCE TEST -- the same measurement that diagnosed the 4S fault" (exclude_from_sim yes) (at 386.08 261.62 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left)) (uuid "d054f0a3-46bc-5ae6-8da7-8b30d596424d"))
  (text "1.  B- to P-  must read a few MILLIvolts.  ~0.55 V means both FETs are\n    off and current is sneaking through the body diodes. That is the\n    exact 4S symptom, and it is what strangled a healthy pack.\n2.  P+ to P-  must equal B3+ to B- within a few mV.\n3.  Each group -- B- to B1+, B1+ to B2+, B2+ to B3+ -- within 50 mV of\n    the others. 12.22 V total is 4.07 V/cell: a full, healthy pack.\n4.  Only then close S1, and only with the motor uncoupled." (exclude_from_sim yes) (at 386.08 278.16 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid "3d871a51-2445-5fc9-90d4-a5739dbb0034"))
  (text "TLS Pie -- Rev 3.0 -- generated by kicad/make_kicad_schematic.py\nEdit the script, not this file. Supersedes Rev 2.0 (WIRING_REV2.html).\nSource of truth for GPIO assignment is tls_stepper.py." (exclude_from_sim yes) (at 386.08 308.62 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid "68527a21-c6df-54da-8c1e-fa6a40ca4a62"))
